Start a run of an eval that has been deployed.

Usage
  azd ai eval run start [flags]

Flags
      --dataset string          : Catalog dataset to read instead of the one the eval declares. Must satisfy the eval's column schema.
      --eval string             : Name of the eval to run, or its id. Defaults to the only one declared.
      --fail-on string          : Fail when the run misses this threshold: any-failure, or pass-rate=<0..1>. pass-rate is measured over the rows that were scored, so rows nothing could grade are outside it; any-failure counts them against the run. Exits 1.
      --max-samples int         : Cap the rows sent from the dataset.
      --name string             : Name for this run. Defaults to the eval name plus a timestamp.
      --no-wait                 : Submit the run and return immediately.
      --path string             : Directory holding azure.eval.yaml. Defaults to the path init used, then ./evals.
      --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint.
      --wait                    : Block until the run reaches a terminal state. (default true)

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for start
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  Start an evaluation and wait for results
    azd ai eval run start --eval quality
